            // Which engine is running, answered by the fact that this line
            // exists.
            //
            // The dispatch used to ask, five times, through eval: `typeof
            // System !== 'undefined' && System.Windows.Forms.Application` and
            // four more like it, each spelled as a string because jsc.exe
            // resolves globals at compile time and would refuse the bare
            // names of engines it is not. That was a run-time test of a
            // compile-time fact. Only jsc.exe compiles this branch, so a
            // program in which this assignment happened *is* the Windows
            // launcher, and nothing has to be detected to know it.
            //
            // Plain JavaScript rather than typed JScript.NET, which the rest
            // of this directory is. It is here because of who compiles it,
            // not because of what it needs to say.
            NeutrinoWebview.runEngine = function () {
                this.runWindows();
            };
